<!--
     SPDX-FileCopyrightText: The LineageOS Project
     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     RRO partition precedence.

     Why this file exists: this device tree's overlays live in /vendor/overlay,
     and by AOSP's default partition order that makes them LOWER priority than
     the GMS overlays in /product/overlay. Measured on the device rather than
     assumed - `cmd overlay list android` prints in increasing priority order and
     puts android.overlay.malbec first, ahead of every
     com.google.android.overlay.pixelconfig*_gms:

         [x] android.overlay.malbec                            <- ours, lowest
         ...
         [x] com.google.android.overlay.pixelconfig2021_gms    <- wins today

     Consequence: any framework resource that both we and a GMS overlay set is
     decided by GMS, silently. The concrete case that surfaced it is
     config_defaultNightMode - PixelConfigOverlay2021_GMS sets it to 2
     (MODE_NIGHT_YES), which is why the device comes up in dark mode even though
     AOSP's own default (config.xml:898) is 1. On this panel - an LCD, not OLED -
     dark mode costs contrast and buys no power, and the device owner cannot read
     it. Simply adding the resource to FrameworkOverlayMalbec would NOT have
     worked; it would have lost.

     The mechanism is AOSP's own: OverlayConfig.PARTITION_ORDER_FILE_PATH is
     hardcoded to "/product/overlay/partition_order.xml"
     (frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/content/om/OverlayConfig.java:76)
     and sortPartitions() reorders the partition list from it, which is why this
     is copied to the product partition even though it is a device-tree file.

     Format constraints, from parseAndValidatePartitionsOrderXml() (:232-288):
       - root element must be <partition-order>
       - every partition must be listed exactly once; a duplicate, a missing one,
         or a count mismatch against PackagePartitions.SYSTEM_PARTITIONS makes
         the whole file be IGNORED with only a Log.w, so a typo here fails silent
       - the names are Build.Partition.PARTITION_NAME_* (Build.java:1747-1759):
         system, vendor, odm, oem, product, system_ext
       - document order is priority order, LOWER first

     The only change from AOSP's default (system, vendor, odm, oem, product,
     system_ext) is that vendor moves from second to just after product. That is
     the minimum edit that puts this device tree above the generic Pixel config
     overlays while leaving system_ext highest, and it is the correct semantic
     for a port: a device-specific overlay should outrank a generic one.

     Blast radius was measured before making the change, not estimated.

     ⚠️ The measurement below has been redone and the old wording was wrong in
     both numbers and conclusion. It said "Our three overlays define 71
     resources; the product overlays define 595; the intersection is EMPTY. So
     today this reorder changes exactly nothing except making the night-mode
     override possible."

     Re-measured with aapt2 against the built APKs: there are FIVE overlays, not
     three, defining 76 resources (35/2/1/2/36), and the intersection is NOT
     empty: product/overlay/PixelConfigOverlay2021_GMS.apk also defines
     integer/config_defaultNightMode. That is the one resource in the overlap,
     and it is the one this reorder exists for, so the reorder is LOAD-BEARING
     rather than a no-op with a side effect. (malbec sets 1, PixelConfig sets 2,
     and framework-res.apk itself already ships 2 from
     vendor/lineage/overlay/common/.../config.xml:150.)

     The distinction matters for anyone considering reverting this file: doing so
     does not merely lose night mode, it hands that resource back to a generic
     GMS overlay. Re-check the intersection if a future GMS bump adds resources -
     the check is:
         for a in vendor/overlay/*.apk product/overlay/*.apk; do
             aapt2 dump resources "$a" | grep -oE 'resource 0x[0-9a-f]+ [a-z-]+/[A-Za-z_0-9]+'
         done
     and compare the two sets.

     Verify after flashing with:
         adb shell cmd overlay list android
     android.overlay.malbec must now appear AFTER the pixelconfig*_gms entries,
     and
         adb shell cmd overlay lookup android android:integer/config_defaultNightMode
     must return 1.
-->
<partition-order>
    <partition name="system" />
    <partition name="odm" />
    <partition name="oem" />
    <partition name="product" />
    <partition name="vendor" />
    <partition name="system_ext" />
</partition-order>
